From: mscharged-port
Subject: New runtime: draw-done without waiting for the render worker
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance (feat/performance). Apply after 0125.

After 0123 the FIFO consumer still waited at every draw-done token until the
render worker had recorded and submitted the packet, so the game emitted its
next frame only after the render worker's tail (Dawn's Vulkan recording at
Submit). The new runtime latches the draw-done once the packet is queued on
the render worker, which records and submits packets in order; the two frame
slots bound how far recording runs ahead.

The VI may present a display copy only after its packet is queued: a copy
recorded in the new runtime becomes eligible when its packet is queued, so a
present (queued on the same worker afterwards) runs on the GPU after it.

The GPU commands and their order are unchanged.

